 of the Rhineland - The National Archives\",\"description\":\"On 7 March 1936 German troops re-occupied the Rhineland, a de-militarised zone according to the Treaty of Versailles. This action was directly against the terms ...Tasks · Background · Teachers' notes\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/education/resources/german-occupation/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"154\",\"title\":\"Hitler reoccupies the Rhineland, violating the Treaty of Versailles\",\"description\":\"Feb 9, 2010 · In 1935, Hitler unilaterally canceled the military clauses of the treaty and in March 1936 denounced the Locarno Pact and began remilitarizing ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.history.com/this-day-in-history/march-7/hitler-reoccupies-the-rhineland\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"155\",\"title\":\"The Anschluss - Jewish Virtual Library\",\"description\":\"(March 12, 1938) The idea of an Anschluss (a united Austria and Germany that would form a “Greater Germany”) began after the unification of Germany excluded ...\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://www.jewishvirtuallibrary.org/the-anschluss\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"156\",\"title\":\"Nazi Territorial Aggression: The Anschluss - Holocaust Encyclopedia\",\"description\":\"Timeline: The Anschluss, March 11–13, 1938. The Anschluss took place over three days in March 1938. Even though the Nazi threat to Austria had been clear for ...\",\"url\":\"https://encyclopedia.ushmm.org/content/en/article/nazi-territorial-aggression-the-anschluss\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"157\",\"title\":\"Triumph of Hitler: Nazis Take Austria - The History Place\",\"description\":\"At dawn on Saturday, March 12, 1938, German soldiers in tanks and armored vehicles roared across the German-Austrian border on schedule. They met no resistance.\",\"url\":\"https://www.historyplace.com/worldwar2/triumph/tr-austria.htm\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"158\",\"title\":\"The Avalon Project : Judgement : The Invasion of Austria\",\"description\":\"At daybreak on the 12th March, 1938, German troops marched into Austria, and met with no resistance. It was announced in the German press that Seyss-Inquart ...\",\"url\":\"https://avalon.law.yale.edu/imt/judaus.asp\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"159\",\"title\":\"Anschluss ( Annexation of Austria - 1938) - Clark University\",\"description\":\"Mar 13, 2024 · Historical background:​​ The Anschluss was the annexation of the Federal State of Austria into the German Reich on 12 March 1938.\",\"url\":\"https://www.clarku.edu/centers/holocaust-and-genocide-studies/2024/03/13/anschluss-postcard/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"160\",\"title\":\"Sudetenland | Facts, History, Map, \u0026 Annexation by Hitler | Britannica\",\"description\":\"Aug 29, 2025 · The Sudeten and other Germans in Czechoslovakia numbered about 3,000,000 in the interwar period. Because of its German majority, the Sudetenland ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.britannica.com/place/Sudetenland\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"161\",\"title\":\"Occupation of the Sudetenland - The Holocaust Explained\",\"description\":\"From the 29 – 30 September 1938, the British, French, Italian and German leaders met in Munich to discuss Hitler's demands for the Sudetenland. This ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.theholocaustexplained.org/life-in-nazi-occupied-europe/foreign-policy-and-the-road-to-war/occupation-of-the-sudetenland/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"162\",\"title\":\"Appeasement and 'Peace for Our Time' | New Orleans\",\"description\":\"Oct 15, 2024 · When Chamberlain went to Munich, he had already accepted Hitler's demand for the Sudetenland. The discussion between Hitler and the leaders ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalww2museum.org/war/articles/appeasement-and-peace-our-time\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"163\",\"title\":\"The Munich Agreement (September 29, 1938) - GHDI - Document\",\"description\":\"... Hitler demanded Germany's entry into the Sudetenland on October 1, 1938. Italian Prime Minister Benito Mussolini, however, managed to