history.com/this-day-in-history/august-23/the-hitler-stalin-pact\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"174\",\"title\":\"German-Soviet Nonaggression Pact | History, Facts, \u0026 Significance\",\"description\":\"The end result of the German-Soviet negotiations was the Nonaggression Pact, which was dated August 23 and was signed by Ribbentrop and Molotov in the presence ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.britannica.com/event/German-Soviet-Nonaggression-Pact\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"175\",\"title\":\"How a False Flag Sparked World War Two: The Gleiwitz Incident ...\",\"description\":\"On the evening of 31 August 1939, a seven-man SS team stormed the transmitter station disguised as Polish insurgents.Missing:  Himmler | Show results with:Himmler\",\"url\":\"https://www.historyhit.com/gleiwitz-incident-explained/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"176\",\"title\":\"Germany invades Poland | September 1, 1939 - History.com\",\"description\":\"Germany invaded Poland to regain lost territory and ultimately rule their neighbor to the east. The German invasion of Poland was a primer on how Hitler ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.history.com/this-day-in-history/september-1/germany-invades-poland\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"177\",\"title\":\"How Europe Went To War In 1939 | Imperial War Museums\",\"description\":\"... and France issued their guarantees to defend Poland's independence in March 1939. In April, Hitler ordered preparations for the invasion of Poland. He ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.iwm.org.uk/history/how-europe-went-to-war-in-1939\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"178\",\"title\":\"Britain and France declare war on Germany | September 3, 1939\",\"description\":\"On September 3, 1939, in response to Hitler's invasion of Poland, Britain and France, both allies of the overrun nation declare war on Germany.\",\"url\":\"https://www.history.com/this-day-in-history/september-3/britain-and-france-declare-war-on-germany\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"179\",\"title\":\"Chamberlain announces Britain is at war with Germany - BBC\",\"description\":\"The news that Britain was at war was broken by Prime Minister Neville Chamberlain at 11.15am on Sunday 3 September 1939.\",\"url\":\"https://www.bbc.com/historyofthebbc/anniversaries/september/war-announced\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"180\",\"title\":\"Battle Of France 1940 In WW2 - What You Should Know\",\"description\":\"German troops entered Paris on 14 June. French forces withdrew from the city the day before and it was declared an 'open city' - meaning it would not be ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.iwm.org.uk/history/what-you-need-to-know-about-the-battle-of-france\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"181\",\"title\":\"Manstein Plan - Spartacus Educational\",\"description\":\"Adolf Hitler gave his approval to the Manstein Plan on 17th February, 1940, but it was not activated until the 10th May, when the Luftwaffe bombed Dutch and ...Missing:  Sichelschnitt breakthrough\",\"url\":\"https://spartacus-educational.com/2WWmanstein.htm\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"182\",\"title\":\"Manstein and Sichelschnitt - The History Reader\",\"description\":\"On 17 February 1940 in Berlin there occurred a simple, unassuming event that changed the course of world history. Manstein journeyed to the capital city of the ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.thehistoryreader.com/military-history/manstein-sichelschnitt/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"183\",\"title\":\"The Dunkirk evacuation and the German 'halt' order\",\"description\":\"Jul 11, 2016 · The German decision to halt the advance of the Panzers for three days. This let-off has given rise to the bizarre idea that it was a deliberate decision by ...\",\"url\":\"https://defenceindepth.co/2016/07/11/the-dunkirk-evacuation-and-the-german-halt-order/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"184\",\"title\":\"Dunkirk Evacuation World War 2 - What You Need To Know\",\"description\":\"The weather providing valuable cover from air attack, the harbour mole allowing extra men to embark, and the German halt order giving the Allies valuable time ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.iwm.org.uk/history/what-you-need-to-know-about-the-dunkirk-evacuations\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"185\",\"title\":\"[PDF] DUNKIRK: The German Decision to Stop the Panzers - Western OJS\",\"description\":\"9 Thus, on May 24, Hitler not only cancelled the transfer of the 4th Army, but he ordered it to halt.10. It seems unlikely that the halt order was based on ...\",\"url\":\"https://ojs.lib.uwo.ca/index.php/westernumirror/article/download/16150/12537/39619\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"186\",\"title\":\"Adolf Hitler in Paris | Anne Frank House\",\"description\":\"Adolf Hitler visited Paris on the day after France had signed the armistice. He admired the city's architecture and visited places of interest.\",\"url\":\"https://www.annefrank.org/en/timeline/205/adolf-hitler-in-paris/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"187\",\"title\":\"The Fall of France in the Second World War - English Heritage\",\"description\":\"On 22 June 1940 the French government surrendered to Hitler, just six weeks after the Germans' initial advance westwards. Why did France collapse so ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.english-heritage.org.uk/visit/places/dover-castle/history-and-stories/fall-of-france/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"188\",\"title\":\"Operation 'Barbarossa' And Germany's Failure In The Soviet Union\",\"description\":\"On the 22nd of June 1941, Adolf Hitler launched Operation Barbarossa, Germany's invasion of the Soviet Union. It was the beginning of a campaign that would ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.iwm.org.uk/history/operation-barbarossa-and-germanys-failure-in-the-soviet-union\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"189\",\"title\":\"The Eastern Front: The German War against the Soviet Union\",\"description\":\"Dec 16, 2022 · 1. Adolf Hitler always planned to destroy the Soviet Union and to establish Lebensraum (living space) for the German people in Soviet territory.\",\"url\":\"https://encyclopedia.ushmm.org/content/en/article/the-soviet-union-and-the-eastern-front\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"190\",\"title\":\"Operation Barbarossa - Army University Press\",\"description\":\"May 2, 2022 · The purpose of Operation Barbarossa was to penetrate deeply with armor and airpower and enable armor freedom of maneuver to achieve an ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.armyupress.army.mil/Journals/NCO-Journal/Archives/2022/May/Operation-Barbarrosa/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"191\",\"title\":\"Defeat of Hitler: Catastrophe at Stalingrad - The History Place\",\"description\":\"Regardless, Hitler ordered the attack on Stalingrad to proceed, and at the same time, ordered the oil fields to be taken. He had changed his mind again. Both ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.historyplace.com/worldwar2/defeat/catastrophe-stalingrad.htm\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"192\",\"title\":\"The Axis Powers of World War II - The National WWII Museum\",\"description\":\"Aug 29, 2024 · In September 1940, Germany, Italy, and Japan signed the Tripartite Act pledging mutual military and economic support for one another.\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalww2museum.org/war/articles/axis-powers-world-war-ii\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"193\",\"title\":\"The Tripartite Pact is signed by Germany, Italy and Japan - History.com\",\"description\":\"On September 27, 1940, the Axis powers are formed as Germany, Italy and Japan become allies with the signing of the Tripartite Pact in Berlin.\",\"url\":\"https://www.history.com/this-day-in-history/september-27/the-tripartite-pact-is-signed-by-germany-italy-and-japan\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"194\",\"title\":\"Axis Powers in World War II - Holocaust Encyclopedia\",\"description\":\"Apr 22, 2022 · On September 27, 1940, Germany, Italy, and Japan signed the Tripartite Pact. This pact formalized the alliance between the three countries, ...\",\"url\":\"https://encyclopedia.ushmm.org/content/en/article/axis-powers-in-world-war-ii\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"195\",\"title\":\"A Shared Enmity: Germany, Japan, and the Creation of the Tripartite ...\",\"description\":\"Dec 10, 2021 · On September 27, 1940, they signed the Tripartite Pact. A 10-year deal between the three, the Pact called for each country to offer military ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalww2museum.org/war/articles/germany-japan-tripartite-pact\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"196\",\"title\":\"Hitler's Declaration of War on the United States | New Orleans\",\"description\":\"Dec 10, 2024 · Hitler's announcement of war with the United States marked the end of years of careful maneuvering on the part of the Nazi leader to secure Germany's ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalww2museum.org/war/articles/hitlers-declaration-war-united-states\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"197\",\"title\":\"Germany declares war on the United States | December 11, 1941\",\"description\":\"Adolf Hitler declares war on the United States, bringing America, which had been neutral, into the European conflict.\",\"url\":\"https://www.history.com/this-day-in-history/december-11/germany-declares-war-on-the-united-states\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"198\",\"title\":\"The German Declaration of War with the United States - Avalon Project\",\"description\":\"On September 11, 1941, the President of the United States publicly declared that he had ordered the American Navy and Air Force to shoot on sight at any German ...\",\"url\":\"https://avalon.law.yale.edu/wwii/gerdec41.asp\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"199\",\"title\":\"Adolf Hitler: Speech Declaring War Against the United States\",\"description\":\"He intended, first of all, to force Germany to make war and to make the German U-boat warfare as ineffective as it was in 1915-16. At the same time, he promised ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.jewishvirtuallibrary.org/hitler-s-speech-declaring-war-against-the-united-states\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"200\",\"title\":\"Operation Barbarossa – The Major Errors and Blunders\",\"description\":\"Jun 24, 2016 · The main problem was that the German army had not a sufficient amount of trucks nor trains even before the beginning of Barbarossa. The main ...\",\"url\":\"http://militaryhistoryvisualized.com/operation-barbarossa-the-major-errors-and-blunders/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"201\",\"title\":\"WW2: Why Did Hitler Declare War On America? - HistoryExtra\",\"description\":\"Jan 28, 2021 · Ian Kershaw explores Adolf Hitler's seemingly inexplicable declaration of war against America and considers whether it was a symptom of his rampant megalomania.\",\"url\":\"https://www.historyextra.com/period/second-world-war/why-did-adolf-hitler-declare-war-usa-america-ww2/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"202\",\"title\":\"[PDF] Stalingrad. An Examination of Hitler's Decision to Airlift - DTIC\",\"description\":\"The battle for that city had ended in disas trous defeat, shatter ing the myth of his military “Midas touch,” ending his chances of defeat ing the Red Army, per ...\",\"url\":\"https://apps.dtic.mil/sti/tr/pdf/ADA529777.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"203\",\"title\":\"Hitler's blunder resulted in a devastating defeat for the German Army ...\",\"description\":\"Hitler fatally weakened the offensive, instructing the Sixth Army, under General Friedrich von Paulus, to attack eastward and capture the industrial city of ...\",\"url\":\"https://warfarehistorynetwork.com/article/hitlers-blunder-resulted-in-a-devastating-defeat-for-the-german-army-on-the-eastern-front/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"204\",\"title\":\"Hitler's Greatest Blunders - HistoryNet\",\"description\":\"Feb 1, 2011 · A complete catalog of Hitler's failures as a war chief could fill a thick volume; a dubious honor roll of the worst of them follows.\",\"url\":\"https://www.historynet.com/hitlers-greatest-blunders/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"205\",\"title\":\"Axis powers miscalculated after early advantages in WW II\",\"description\":\"Dec 12, 2017 · Hanson said that Hitler mistakenly assumed that America's isolationism would mean it would not move millions of soldiers to Europe as it had in ...\",\"url\":\"https://news.stanford.edu/stories/2017/12/axis-powers-miscalculated-early-advantages-wwii-stanford-scholar-says\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"206\",\"title\":\"Reply to Darryl Cooper: The Truth About World War II\",\"description\":\"Sep 13, 2024 · In perhaps the war's greatest miscalculation, Hitler believed that the supposedly easier conquest of Russia would then force a completely ...\",\"url\":\"https://winstonchurchill.hillsdale.edu/churchill-cooper-ww2/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"207\",\"title\":\"Hitler descends into his bunker | January 16, 1945 - History.com\",\"description\":\"Adolf Hitler takes to his underground bunker, where he remains for 105 days until he died by suicide. Hitler retired to his bunker after deciding to remain ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.history.com/this-day-in-history/january-16/hitler-descends-into-his-bunker\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"208\",\"title\":\"Hitler's Death in the Führerbunker - Warfare History Network\",\"description\":\"It was the end of April 1945. As he sat in the dank gloom of the Führerbunker deep beneath the garden of the Chancellery in Berlin, Hitler no doubt reflected on ...\",\"url\":\"https://warfarehistorynetwork.com/hitlers-death-in-the-fuhrerbunker/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"209\",\"title\":\"Hitler's last days | MI5 - The Security Service\",\"description\":\"Hitler's adjutant lit a petrol-soaked rag and threw it on the bodies, which immediately burst into flames. The group made the Hitlergruss (the Nazi salute) and ...Missing:  manner | Show results with:manner\",\"url\":\"https://www.mi5.gov.uk/history/world-war-ii/hitlers-last-days\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"210\",\"title\":\"World War II in Europe Timeline: April 30, 1945 - Death of Hitler\",\"description\":\"In April of 1945, Hitler moved into the Führerbunker, located 50 feet below the Chancellery buildings in Berlin.\",\"url\":\"https://www.historyplace.com/worldwar2/timeline/death.htm\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"211\",\"title\":\"Extracts From Mein Kampf by Adolf Hitler | Documents - Yad Vashem\",\"description\":\"Extracts From Mein Kampf by Adolf Hitler ... ...The Jewish doctrine of Marxism rejects the aristocratic principle of Nature and replaces the eternal privilege of ...Missing:  theoretical | Show results with:theoretical\",\"url\":\"https://www.yadvashem.org/docs/extracts-from-mein-kampf.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"212\",\"title\":\"Racism and Antisemitism: Defining the Terms - Yad Vashem\",\"description\":\"The Middle East Conflict, Antisemitism and the Holocaust; Racism and ... In the mid-1850s Comte Arthur de Gobineau published his “Essay on the Inequality of Human ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.yadvashem.org/holocaust/holocaust-antisemitism/racism.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"213\",\"title\":\"Houston Stewart Chamberlain | German Nationalist, Anti-Semite ...\",\"description\":\"Sep 5, 2025 · Houston Stewart Chamberlain was a British-born Germanophile political philosopher, whose advocacy of the racial and cultural superiority of ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.britannica.com/biography/Houston-Stewart-Chamberlain\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"214\",\"title\":\"Race-Thinking, Völkisch-Nationalism, and Eugenics (Chapter 11)\",\"description\":\"May 16, 2025 · This chapter explores the evolution of racial ideas before and after the First World War, comparing German-speaking central Europe with the rest of Europe, the ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.cambridge.org/core/books/cambridge-history-of-the-holocaust/racethinking-volkischnationalism-and-eugenics/81050E973E9748C976304CE25B0F9761\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"215\",\"title\":\"Aryan | Holocaust Encyclopedia\",\"description\":\"Sep 29, 2020 · Adolf Hitler and the Nazi Party adapted, manipulated, and ... Antisemitism in History: Racial Antisemitism, 1875–1945 Article. Nazi ...\",\"url\":\"https://encyclopedia.ushmm.org/content/en/article/aryan-1\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"216\",\"title\":\"The persecution of the Jews / Before the extermination / History ...\",\"description\":\"A boycott of Jewish shops was organized in Germany as early as April 1, 1933. From then on, laws and regulations were regularly issued that systematically ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.auschwitz.org/en/history/before-the-extermination/the-persecution-of-the-jews\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"217\",\"title\":\"A Timeline of the Holocaust (1933 - 1945) - JewishGen\",\"description\":\"January 30: Adolf Hitler appointed Chancellor of Germany by President Von Hindenburg. March 22: The first official Nazi concentration camp opens in Dachau, a ...1933 · 1938 · 1939 · 1941\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://www.jewishgen.org/forgottencamps/general/timeeng.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"218\",\"title\":\"Prewar Nazi Germany and the Beginnings of the Holocaust\",\"description\":\"During the first six years of Hitler's rule, German Jews felt the effects of legislation that transformed them from “citizens” to “outcasts.”\",\"url\":\"https://encyclopedia.ushmm.org/content/en/timeline-group/holocaust/1933-1938\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"219\",\"title\":\"Rise of the Nazis and Beginning of Persecution - Yad Vashem\",\"description\":\"Hitler and the Nazi Party rose to power due to the social and political circumstances that characterized the interwar period in Germany.\",\"url\":\"https://www.yadvashem.org/holocaust/about/nazi-germany-1933-39/beginning-of-persecution.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"220\",\"title\":\"Nuremberg race laws imposed | September 15, 1935 - History.com\",\"description\":\"On September 15, 1935, German Jews are stripped of their citizenship, reducing them to mere “subjects” of the state. ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.history.com/this-day-in-history/september-15/nuremberg-race-laws-imposed\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"221\",\"title\":\"The Nuremberg Race Laws | Anne Frank House\",\"description\":\"On 15 September 1935, the Nazis introduced the