/features/goebbels-himmler/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"258\",\"title\":\"Heinrich Himmler: The Rise and Fall of Hitler's Third Reichsführer-SS\",\"description\":\"Dec 27, 2021 · From Hitler loyalist to anti-Hitler plotter, the wily Nazi SS chief played a double game in 1945–just as he always had.\",\"url\":\"https://warfarehistorynetwork.com/article/heinrich-himmler-the-rise-and-fall-of-hitlers-third-reichsfuhrer-ss/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"259\",\"title\":\"Hitler's Better Half | Foreign Affairs\",\"description\":\"Hess became Hitler's mirror and sloganeer. His relationship to him can be characterized only as admiration and love, though the customary suspicion that has ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.foreignaffairs.com/germany/hitlers-better-half\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"260\",\"title\":\"Deputy Führer Rudolf Hess: Foe or Ally? - Warfare History Network\",\"description\":\"Throughout his career as a member of the Nazi Party, until his final days in Spandau, Rudolf Hess remained a loyal follower of Adolf Hitler. Even after the war ...\",\"url\":\"https://warfarehistorynetwork.com/article/deputy-fuhrer-rudolf-hess-foe-or-ally/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"261\",\"title\":\"Martin Bormann and Adolf Hitler on the Berghof Terrace (1942)\",\"description\":\"The extent to which Bormann enjoyed Hitler's confidence is made clear, for example, by the fact that Hitler entrusted him with the management of his own private ...\",\"url\":\"https://ghdi.ghi-dc.org/sub_image.cfm?image_id=2327\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"262\",\"title\":\"Hitler's Inner Circle: The 7 Most Powerful Figures in the Third Reich\",\"description\":\"Jun 5, 2024 · Officially, Martin Bormann (1900-1945) was Chief of the Party Chancellery and Personal Secretary to the Führer. Unofficially, he was Hitler's ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.thecollector.com/hitler-circle-powerful-figures-third-reich/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"263\",\"title\":\"Albert Speer - Hitler's architect and armaments chief - Alpha History\",\"description\":\"In 1934 Speer became the NSDAP's chief architect and his relationship with Hitler blossomed into friendship. During the mid-1930s Speer designed and ...\",\"url\":\"https://alphahistory.com/nazigermany/albert-speer/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"264\",\"title\":\"Albert Speer: Architect, Minister, and Hitler's Closest Friend\",\"description\":\"Jul 14, 2024 · By 1939, the two had developed an unlikely friendship, with Speer now very much a part of Hitler's inner circle. Along with a select few others, ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.thecollector.com/albert-speer-architect-minister-hitler-friend/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"265\",\"title\":\"The Candor and Lies of Nazi Officer Albert Speer\",\"description\":\"Jan 8, 2013 · Speer said he was furious and disobeyed Hitler's orders, transferring his loyalty from der Fuhrer to the German people and the future of the ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.smithsonianmag.com/history/the-candor-and-lies-of-nazi-officer-albert-speer-324737/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"266\",\"title\":\"Hindenburg and Hitler — How Germany's War-Hero President Set ...\",\"description\":\"Jan 25, 2022 · On January 30, 1933, Hindenburg appointed Hitler chancellor of Germany. It has been widely reported that the president was senile or unwell when he made this ...\",\"url\":\"https://militaryhistorynow.com/2022/01/25/hindenburg-and-hitler-how-germanys-war-hero-president-set-the-stage-for-a-nazi-takeover/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"267\",\"title\":\"President Paul von Hindenburg's Role in Hitler's Rise to Power\",\"description\":\"Jul 12, 2023 · Although he was hailed as a symbol of stability, and disapproved of Hitler and his politics, Hindenburg's decisions and actions as president ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.historyhit.com/president-paul-von-hindenburgs-role-in-hitlers-rise-to-power/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"268\",\"title\":\"Hitler and Mussolini - Alpha History\",\"description\":\"Hitler and Mussolini were thrust together as cautious, sometimes suspicious allies - Italian fascism being the 'older brother' of Nazism.Early admiration · Mussolini's scorn · Racial views · Nazi support in Abyssinia\",\"url\":\"https://alphahistory.com/nazigermany/hitler-and-mussolini/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"269\",\"title\":\"The relationship between Mussolini and Hitler was not always one ...\",\"description\":\"Mussolini was impressed with Hitler's bold reoccupation of the Rhineland. He also became convinced that the British and French could not be counted on.\",\"url\":\"https://warfarehistorynetwork.com/article/the-relationship-between-mussolini-and-hitler-was-not-always-one-of-mutual-admiration/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"270\",\"title\":\"[PDF] Nazi Art, Adolf Hitler, and the Cult of Personality. - ARSOF History\",\"description\":\"The Führer, Adolf Hitler, portrayed as the military leader of Germany. “Cult of Personality”. Unless otherwise noted the artwork featured in this article is ...Missing:  construction | Show results with:construction\",\"url\":\"https://arsof-history.org/articles/pdf/v4n2_creating_a_demigod.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"271\",\"title\":\"cult of personality | Experiencing History\",\"description\":\"cult of personality. Nazi propaganda often focused on glorifying Adolf Hitler as Germany's sole savior in order to inspire a sense of personal devotion to him.Missing:  construction | Show results with:construction\",\"url\":\"https://perspectives.ushmm.org/tag/cult-of-personality\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"272\",\"title\":\"Nazi Propaganda and National Unity - Experiencing History\",\"description\":\"The Role of Propaganda in Building the Nazi National Community. Nazi ... propaganda also promoted a cult of personality around Nazi leader Adolf Hitler.Missing:  construction | Show results with:construction\",\"url\":\"https://perspectives.ushmm.org/collection/nazi-propaganda-and-national-unity\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"273\",\"title\":\"How the Nazis used poster art as propaganda – DW – 11/30/2020\",\"description\":\"Nov 30, 2020 · \\\"One people, one Reich, one leader!\\\" was the motto projected on many of the posters that cemented the personality cult around Adolf Hitler. But ...Missing:  construction | Show results with:construction\",\"url\":\"https://www.dw.com/en/how-the-nazis-used-poster-art-as-propaganda/a-55751640\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"274\",\"title\":\"Nazi Germany's Schriftleitergesetz: The End of Freedom of the Press\",\"description\":\"Oct 4, 2021 · “I have the natural intention to be and to remain the warm-hearted protector of the German press.” These are the words Propaganda Minister ...\",\"url\":\"https://arolsen-archives.org/en/news/nazi-germanys-schriftleitergesetz-the-end-of-freedom-of-the-press/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"275\",\"title\":\"Nazi Propaganda and Censorship | Holocaust Encyclopedia\",\"description\":\"Sep 23, 2025 · The Nazis wanted Germans to support the Nazi dictatorship and believe in Nazi ideas. To accomplish this goal, they tried to control forms of ...\",\"url\":\"https://encyclopedia.ushmm.org/content/en/article/nazi-propaganda-and-censorship\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"276\",\"title\":\"Alois Hitler | father of Adolf Hitler | Britannica\",\"description\":\"Sep 24, 2025 · Hitler's father, Alois (born 1837), was illegitimate. For a time he bore his mother's name, Schicklgruber, but by 1876 he had established his family claim to ...Missing:  paternity | Show results with:paternity\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://www.britannica.com/biography/Alois-Hitler\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"277\",\"title\":\"Who Was Adolf Hitler's Mother? The Little-Known Story Of Klara Hitler\",\"description\":\"Jan 26, 2023 · Born Klara Pölzl in Austria in 1860, the mother of Adolf Hitler had an unusually close relationship with her son, and her death in 1907 ...\",\"url\":\"https://allthatsinteresting.com/klara-hitler\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"278\",\"title\":\"Rise of Hitler: Hitler's Mother Dies - The History Place\",\"description\":\"On January 14, 1907, Adolf Hitler's mother went to see the family doctor about a pain in her chest, so bad it kept her awake at night.\",\"url\":\"https://www.historyplace.com/worldwar2/riseofhitler/mother.htm\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"279\",\"title\":\"Paula Hitler: The Surprisingly Quiet Life Of Adolf's Little Sister\",\"description\":\"Aug 7, 2019 · Hitler's younger sister, Paula Hitler (1896-1960), lived a quiet life under the name Wolff despite having perhaps been a Nazi sympathizer ...\",\"url\":\"https://allthatsinteresting.com/paula-hitler\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"280\",\"title\":\"Hitler's half-brother married a Dublin woman in 1910, census shows\",\"description\":\"Apr 13, 2023 · Adolf Hitler's half-brother Alois Hitler married Dublin native Bridget Dowling in 1910 and the two went on to have a son, Patrick William.\",\"url\":\"https://www.irishcentral.com/roots/genealogy/hitler-brother-married-dublin-woman\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"281\",\"title\":\"Adolf Hitler's Family Tree - ThoughtCo\",\"description\":\"Sep 27, 2018 · Rosenberg, Jennifer. \\\"Adolf Hitler's Family Tree.\\\" ThoughtCo, Apr. 5, 2023, thoughtco.com/hitlers-family-tree-1779646. Rosenberg, Jennifer. ( ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.thoughtco.com/hitlers-family-tree-1779646\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"282\",\"title\":\"Geli Raubal: Adolf Hitler's Niece And His Romantic Obsession\",\"description\":\"Feb 25, 2023 · Found dead in his Munich apartment on September 18, 1931, Geli Raubal was Adolf Hitler's niece who many historians believe had a romantic relationship with the ...\",\"url\":\"https://allthatsinteresting.com/geli-raubal\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"283\",\"title\":\"\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://www.vanityfair.com/news/1992/04/hitlers-doomed-angel\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"284\",\"title\":\"Adolf Hitler and Eva Braun marry | April 29, 1945 - History.com\",\"description\":\"During t