\":\"The Italian and German fascist regimes were eager to lay claim to Nietzsche's ideas, and to position themselves as inspired by them. In 1932, Nietzsche's sister ...\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Influence_and_reception_of_Friedrich_Nietzsche\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"307\",\"title\":\"Hitler, Mein Kampf, 1926 - Hanover College History Department\",\"description\":\"Adolf Hitler Mein Kampf (1926). In 1923 Adolf Hitler was arrested for attempting to overthrow the government in Munich. His National Socialist German Workers ...Missing:  primary sources\",\"url\":\"https://history.hanover.edu/courses/excerpts/111hitler.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"308\",\"title\":\"Nazi spiritual eugenics (II): Hitler and the Will of Nature\",\"description\":\"Hitler sees evolution guided by Providence, favouring the higher race in their spiritual mission ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.philosophyforlife.org/blog/nazi-spiritual-eugenics-ii-hitler-and-the-will-of-nature\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"309\",\"title\":\"The Last Days of Hitler - The University of Chicago Press\",\"description\":\"focuses on the last ten days of Hitler's life, April 20-29, 1945, in the underground bunker in Berlin—a bizarre and gripping episode ...\",\"url\":\"https://press.uchicago.edu/ucp/books/book/chicago/L/bo3626997.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"310\",\"title\":\"Nuremberg - Explore the Nuremberg Trials!\",\"description\":\"Search thousands of historical documents from the Nuremberg trials. Examine trial transcripts, briefs, document books, evidence files, and other papersDocuments · Access all the trials · About the Project · People\",\"url\":\"https://nuremberg.law.harvard.edu/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"311\",\"title\":\"The Nuremberg Trials | The National WWII Museum | New Orleans\",\"description\":\"The trials uncovered the German leadership that supported the Nazi dictatorship. Of the 177 defendants, 24 were sentenced to death, 20 to ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalww2museum.org/war/topics/nuremberg-trials\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"312\",\"title\":\"Evidence from the Holocaust at the First Nuremberg Trial\",\"description\":\"Dec 15, 2020 · German documents and the testimony of German officials presented at the Nuremberg trial revealed and documented considerable information about the Holocaust.\",\"url\":\"https://encyclopedia.ushmm.org/content/en/article/evidence-from-the-holocaust\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"313\",\"title\":\"Analysis of the Personality of Adolph Hitler | Donovan Nuremberg ...\",\"description\":\"Analysis of the Personality of Adolph Hitler is a report by pioneering Harvard psychologist Dr. Henry A. Murray, prepared for the Office of Strategic Services ...\",\"url\":\"https://digital.library.cornell.edu/collections/nuremberg/analysis-hitler\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"314\",\"title\":\"[PDF] A PSYCHOLOGICAL ANALYSIS OF ADOLPH HITLER HIS ... - CIA\",\"description\":\"This belief in his own power actually borders on a feeling of omnipotence which he is not reluctant to display. It is also indicative that Hitler, some time ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.cia.gov/readingroom/docs/CIA-RDP78-02646R000600240001-5.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"315\",\"title\":\"[PDF] Public opinion in occupied Germany: the OMGUS surveys, 1945-1949\",\"description\":\"... IMMEDIATE OCCUPATION POLICIES. 9. Attitudes toward the American Occupation ... Hitler's Germany, the Intelligence. Branch of the Office of the Director of.\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://libsysdigi.library.uiuc.edu/OCA/Books2009-07/publicopinionino00merr/publicopinionino00merr.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"316\",\"title\":\"FBI Records: The Vault — Adolf Hitler\",\"description\":\"At the time, it was feared that Hitler may have escaped in the closing days of the war, and searches were made to determine if he was still alive. FBI Files ...Adolf Hitler Part 01 · Adolf Hitler Part 02 · ViewMissing:  assessments | Show results with:assessments\",\"url\":\"https://vault.fbi.gov/adolf-hitler\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"317\",\"title\":\"How Did Germany Respond to the Great Depression? - Facing History\",\"description\":\"Aug 2, 2016 · All in all, the program helped to increase public support for the Nazis, as Evans explains: Hitler's boast that he would solve the unemployment ...Missing:  electoral | Show results with:electoral\",\"url\":\"https://www.facinghistory.org/resource-library/battle-work\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"318\",\"title\":\"[PDF] CRISIS IN NAZI GERMANY, 1933-1937 - ifo Institut\",\"description\":\"We compare trends in mortality, nutritional status and food supply to other living standard indicators for the early years of the Nazi period.\",\"url\":\"https://www.ifo.de/DocDL/cesifo_wp800.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"319\",\"title\":\"Autobahn Construction During the Nazi Regime\",\"description\":\"Planners completed 3,800 kilometers (with an initial goal of 7,000) of the Autobahn by 1941, when the Nazis suspended all plans due to dwindling resources. The ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.environmentandsociety.org/tools/keywords/autobahn-construction-during-nazi-regime\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"320\",\"title\":\"[PDF] R.-J.-Overy-1982.The-Nazi-Economic-Recovery-1932–1938 ...\",\"description\":\"The rise of Nazism and its final consolidation of political power between 1933 and 1936 was bound up with the failure of the Weimar governments' economic ...Missing:  GDP | Show results with:GDP\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://lburlamaqui.com.br/wp-content/uploads/2021/02/R.-J.-Overy-1982.The-Nazi-Economic-Recovery-1932%25E2%2580%25931938-Macmillan-Education-UK-.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"321\",\"title\":\"[PDF] The German Army in World War II\",\"description\":\"The Army was the largest arm, averaging about 75% of total Wehrmacht strength, with 2,700,000 troops in September 1939, reaching a maximum strength of about ...\",\"url\":\"https://prussia.online/Data/Book/th/the-german-army-in-world-war-ii/General%2520Military%2520-%2520The%2520German%2520Army%2520in%2520World%2520War%2520II.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"322\",\"title\":\"Build up to war – The Holocaust Explained: Designed for schools\",\"description\":\"Under this agreement, Germany could expand its navy to 35% of the size of the British Navy. Britain made this agreement in order to avoid a major naval arms ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.theholocaustexplained.org/life-in-nazi-occupied-europe/foreign-policy-and-the-road-to-war/build-up-to-war/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"323\",\"title\":\"Blitzkrieg Unleashed: Germany Invades Poland 1939 refers to the ...\",\"description\":\"Jun 16, 2025 · The strategy, known as \\\"Blitzkrieg\\\" or \\\"lightning war,\\\" combined fast-moving and coordinated attacks using infantry, tanks, and air support to overwhelm the ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.facebook.com/KingsGenerals/posts/blitzkrieg-unleashed-germany-invades-poland-1939-refers-to-the-rapid-military-ca/1146363837531690/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"324\",\"title\":\"Blitzkrieg 1940: From the Invasion of Holland to the Fall of France\",\"description\":\"Panzer Breakthrough in the Ardennes. Throughout the morning, Heinkel bombers dropped their loads on railway junctions and air bases in northeastern France ...\",\"url\":\"https://warfarehistorynetwork.com/article/blitzkrieg-1940-from-the-invasion-of-holland-to-the-fall-of-france/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"325\",\"title\":\"The German 'Lightning War' Strategy Of The Second World War\",\"description\":\"World War 2: Blitzkrieg, meaning 'Lightning War', was the method of offensive warfare responsible for Nazi Germany's military successes in early WW2.Missing:  achievements | Show results with:achievements\",\"url\":\"https://www.iwm.org.uk/history/the-german-lightning-war-strategy-of-the-second-world-war\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"326\",\"title\":\"Enabling Act | 1933, Definition, Adolf Hitler, \u0026 Third Reich | Britannica\",\"description\":\"Sep 24, 2025 · Enabling Act, law passed by the German Reichstag on March 23, 1933, that enabled Chancellor Adolf Hitler to assume dictatorial powers.\",\"url\":\"https://www.britannica.com/topic/Enabling-Act\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"327\",\"title\":\"The Enabling Act: even more power for Hitler | Anne Frank House\",\"description\":\"On 23 March 1933, the German parliament voted in favour of the 'Enabling Act ... This law allowed Hitler to rule Germany as a dictator from then on. No ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.annefrank.org/en/timeline/48/the-enabling-act-even-more-power-for-hitler/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"328\",\"title\":\"Why the Nazis were able to stay in power Establishing a totalitarian ...\",\"description\":\"Under Hitler, the Nazis tried to take total control of Germany through a range of measures: crushing of opposition; fear and state terrorism; social controls ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.bbc.co.uk/bitesize/guides/zgtyvcw/revision/1\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"329\",\"title\":\"Night of the Long Knives | Date, Victims, Summary, \u0026 Facts | Britannica\",\"description\":\"Sep 24, 2025 · Night of the Long Knives, in German history, purge of Nazi leaders by Adolf Hitler on June 30, 1934. Fearing that the paramilitary SA had ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.britannica.com/event/Night-of-the-Long-Knives\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"330\",\"title\":\"Evidence and Documentation of the Holocaust\",\"description\":\"Documenting Numbers of Victims of the Holocaust and Nazi Persecution. The Holocaust is the best documented case of genocide. Anne Frank. The story of Anne ...Nazi Germany · Gassing Operations · \\\"Final Solution\\\": Overview\",\"url\":\"https://www.ushmm.org/antisemitism/holocaust-denial-and-distortion/evidence-documentation-holocaust\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"331\",\"title\":\"Nazism - Totalitarianism, Expansionism, Fascism | Britannica\",\"description\":\"Through both successful electioneering and intimidation, the party came to power in Germany in 1933 and governed through totalitarian methods until 1945, when ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.britannica.com/event/Nazism/Totalitarianism-and-expansionism\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"332\",\"title\":\"The Selling of Adolf Hitler: David Irving's Hitler's War\",\"description\":\"Dec 16, 2008 · The field of studies focusing on Adolf Hitler and the National Socialist period of German history has been invaded and nearly overrun by an international ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/central-european-history/article/selling-of-adolf-hitler-david-irvings-hitlers-war/57C8052685E48F6507791629102EFB6B\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"333\",\"title\":\"Adolf Hitler: Hitler's Orders - Holocaust Denial on Trial\",\"description\":\"It is highly probable that there is no written order from Adolf Hitler authorizing the extermination of the Jews.\u003c|control11|\u003e\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://www.hdot.org/debunking-denial/ah1-hitlers-orders/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"334\",\"title\":\"Joe Rogan hosts Holocaust revisionist on his podcast, complains of ...\",\"description\":\"Mar 15, 2025 · He claimed, among other things, that Hitler opposed the mass 1938 Kristallnacht pogrom and that Hitler came to be antisemitic from feeling the ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.timesofisrael.com/joe-rogan-hosts-holocaust-revisionist-on-his-podcast-complains-of-paranoid-jews/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"335\",\"title\":\"David Irving - Southern Poverty Law Center\",\"description\":\"But since the 1980s, he has cultivated a reputation as the world's most prominent Holocaust denier, a status he cemented by suing Penguin Books and American ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.splcenter.org/resources/extremist-files/david-irving/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"336\",\"title\":\"The historiography of Nazi Germany - Alpha History\",\"description\":\"A small clique of revisionist historians went even further, offering sympathetic accounts of Hitler and suggesting that he has been poorly treated by history ...\",\"url\":\"https://alphahistory.com/nazigermany/historiography-of-nazi-germany/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"337\",\"title\":\"Irving: consigned to history as a racist liar | Books - The Guardian\",\"description\":\"Apr 12, 2000 · The author David Irving falsified history to exonerate Adolf Hitler, driven by anti-Semitism and his own pro-Nazi views, the high court ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.theguardian.com/books/2000/apr/12/uk.irving\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"338\",\"title\":\"Leuchter Report / Holocaust denial / History / Auschwitz-Birkenau\",\"description\":\"Leuchter states that there were far fewer compounds of hydrogen cyanide in the walls of the gas chambers at Auschwitz than in the walls of the disinfection ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.auschwitz.org/en/history/holocaust-denial/leuchter-report/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"339\",\"title\":\"Nazi social and economic policies - National 5 History Revision - BBC\",\"description\":\"Economic policies ... The Nazis tried to make Germany self-sufficient - that is to produce all the goods it needed without having to rely on imported supplies.Missing:  revisionism | Show results with:revisionism\",\"url\":\"https://www.bbc.co.uk/bitesize/guides/zsdfr82/revision/2\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"340\",\"title\":\"The troubling rise of Hitler revisionism - Slow Boring\",\"description\":\"Apr 14, 2025 · The troubling rise of Hitler revisionism. The New Right wants to destigmatize bigotry, and it's bad. Matthew Yglesias's avatar · Matthew ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.slowboring.com/p/the-troubling-rise-of-hitler-revisionism\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"341\",\"title\":\"Cold Conflict | The National WWII Museum | New Orleans\",\"description\":\"Following the defeat of the Axis powers, an ideological and political rivalry between the United States and the USSR gave way to the start of the Cold War.\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalww2museum.org/war/articles/cold-conflict\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"342\",\"title\":\"Holocaust Survivors and the Establishment of the State of Israel ...\",\"description\":\"Jan 2, 2025 · Beginning in May 1948, tens of thousands of Holocaust survivors rebuilt their lives in the newly established State of Israel.\",\"url\":\"https://encyclopedia.ushmm.org/content/en/article/postwar-refugee-crisis-and-the-establishment-of-the-state-of-israel\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"343\",\"title\":\"The Holocaust and the Founding of Israel (July 1998)\",\"description\":\"Hitler's policy of genocide against European Jews during World War II and its relationship to the subsequent founding of the state of Israel in 1948.\",\"url\":\"https://www.loc.gov/loc/lcib/9807/aronson.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"344\",\"title\":\"The Holocaust: Factor in the Birth of Israel? - Yad Vashem\",\"description\":\"It is widely believed that the catastrophe of European Jewry during World War II had a decisive influence on the establishment of the Jewish state in 1948.\",\"url\":\"https://www.yadvashem.org/articles/academic/holocaust-factor-birth.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"345\",\"title\":\"History of the European Union – 1945-59\",\"description\":\"The Second World War ends in Europe. The continent is devastated. Millions of people are dead, injured or displaced. Six million Jews have been murdered in the ...\",\"url\":\"https://european-union.europa.eu/principles-countries-history/history-eu/1945-59_en\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"346\",\"title\":\"[PDF] The Impact of the Second World War on the Decolonization of Africa\",\"description\":\"World War II led to decolonization of Africa by affecting both Europe and Africa militarily, psychologically, politically, and economically. In 1939, Nazi ...\",\"url\":\"https://scholarworks.bgsu.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1048\u0026context=africana_studies_conf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"347\",\"title\":\"Marshall Plan, 1948 - Office of the Historian\",\"description\":\"The Marshall Plan generated a resurgence of European industrialization and brought extensive investment into the region.\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://history.state.gov/milestones/1945-1952/marshall-plan\",\"favicon\":\"\"}],\"images\":[{\"id\":\"f538f72f2838\",\"caption\":\"Black-and-white photographic portrait of Hitler standing\",\"url\":\"./_assets_/Hitler_portrait_crop.jpg\",\"position\":\"CENTER\",\"width\":0,\"height\":0},{\"id\":\"b5078089dc5a\",\"caption\":\"Alois Hitler in his last years\",\"url\":\"./_assets_/Alois_Hitler_in_his_last_years_2.jpg\",\"position\":\"CENTER\",\"width\":0,\"height\":0},{\"id\":\"4054b8cce0f6\",\"caption\":\"Hitler family house in Leonding\",\"url\":\"./_assets_/Hitler_house_in_Leonding.jpg\",\"position\":\"CENTER\",\"width\":0,\"height\":0},{\"id\":\"4054b8cce0f6\",\"caption\":\"Hitler house in Leonding\",\"url\":\"./_assets_/Hitler_house_in_Leonding.jpg\",\"position\":\"CENTER\",\"width\":0,\"height\":0},{\"id\":\"6fa6b0720f9a\",\"caption\":\"Painting of Munich's Der Alte Hof courtyard by Adolf Hitler\",\"url\":\"./_assets_/Adolf_Hitler_Der_Alte_Hof.jpg\",\"position\":\"CENTER\",\"width\":0,\"height\":0},{\"id\":\"0d3b0f85c2d3\",\"caption\":\"Adolf Hitler in World War I uniform\",\"url\":\"./_assets_/Bundesarchiv_Bild_146-1974-082-44%252C_Adolf_Hitler_im_Ersten_Weltkrieg_retouched.jpg\",\"position\":\"CENTER\",\"width\":0,\"height\":0},{\"id\":\"46bc0b6b23de\",\"caption\":\"Bundesarchiv Bild 146-1974-082-44, Adolf Hitler im Ersten Weltkrieg retouched\",\"url\":\"._assets_/Bundesarchiv_Bild_146-1974-082-44%252C_Adolf_Hitler_im_Ersten_Weltkrieg_retouched.jpg\",\"position\":\"CENTER\",\"width\":0,\"height\":0},{\"id\":\"0a23d92dd3a4\",\"caption\":\"Hitler's DAP membership card\",\"url\":\"./_assets_/Hitler's_DAP_membership_card.png\",\"position\":\"CENTER\",\"width\":0,\"height\":0},{\"id\":\"8157f6af1f9e\",\"caption\":\"Black-and-white photograph of Adolf Hitler in a dynamic speaking pose during early Nazi rallies\",\"url\":\"./_assets_/Bundesarchiv_Bild_102-10460%252C_Adolf_Hitler%252C_Rednerposen.jpg\",\"position\":\"CENTER\",\"width\":0,\"height\":0},{\"id\":\"e7c052194a16\",\"caption\":\"Adolf Hitler after the Hitler-Ludendorff trial\",\"url\":\"./_assets_/Bundesarchiv_Bild_102-00344A%252C_M%C3%BCnchen%252C_nach_Hitler-Ludendorff_Prozess.jpg\",\"position\":\"CENTER\",\"width\":0,\"height\":0},{\"id\":\"904b3af8f468\",\"caption\":\"Dust jacket of Mein Kampf\",\"url\":\"./_assets_/Mein_Kampf_dust_jacket.jpeg\",\"position\":\"CENTER\",\"width\":0,\"height\":0},{\"id\":\"912c6d029fd9\",\"caption\":\"Hitler at the inauguration of the Brown House, the NSDAP headquarters in Munich, 1928\",\"url\":\"./_assets_/Bundesarchiv_Bild_119-0289%252C_M%C3%BCnchen%252C_Hitler_bei_Einweihung_%22Braunes_Haus%22.jpg\",\"position\":\"CENTER\",\"width\":0,\"height\":0},{\"id\":\"8157f6af1f9e\",\"caption\":\"Adolf Hitler delivering a speech at a rally\",\"url\":\"./_assets_/Bundesarchiv_Bild_102-10460%252C_Adolf_Hitler%252C_Rednerposen.jpg\",\"position\":\"CENTER\",\"width\":0,\"height\":0},{\"id\":\"c2cc92aa3ae9\",\"caption\":\"Adolf Hitler during the Machtübernahme\",\"url\":\"._assets_/Bundesarchiv_Bild_146-1972-026-11%252C_Macht%C3%BCbernahme_Hitlers.jpg\",\"position\":\"CENTER\",\"width\":0,\"height\":0},{\"id\":\"d4ef16845ee0\",\"caption\":\"Hitler during the Machtergreifung\",\"url\":\"./_assets_/Bundesarchiv_Bild_146-1972-026-11%252C_Macht%C3%BCbernahme_Hitlers.jpg\",\"position\":\"CENTER\",\"width\":0,\"height\":0},{\"id\":\"889282fc81e6\",\"caption\":\"Nuremberg Party Rally\",\"url\":\"./_assets_/Bundesarchiv_Bild_102-04062A%252C_N%C3%BCrnberg%252C_Reichsparteitag%252C_SA-_und_SS-Appell.jpg\",\"position\":\"CENTER\",\"width\":0,\"height\":0},{\"id\":\"7e4966be9049\",\"caption\":\"Benito Mussolini and Adolf Hitler\",\"url\":\"._assets_/Benito_Mussolini_and_Adolf_Hitler.jpg\",\"position\":\"CENTER\",\"width\":0,\"height\":0},{\"id\":\"0a94e7231393\",\"caption\":\"Hitler visiting E